<Ui>
    <!--
        BENILLA_ALLOW_OWN_UI=1 — the director's two LOOK deviations on the pet page's autocast
        button, over the reference's own SpellBookFrame.xml (decisions 1392/1393; re-seated by 2014
        onto the reference's own Model now that this engine renders it — 2013).

        Since 2013 the `$parentAutoCast` <Model> on every SpellButton draws its own file
        (Interface\Buttons\UI-AutoCastButton.mdx) as a tile: four bones chasing the corners of a
        0.02-unit square, four spline emitters trailing GlowStar sparks off them, on the pane's own
        clock. The reference declares it 36x36 at CENTER (1,1) at scale 1.22 — a 0.87x rim that
        floats clear of the viewport edge, never clipped, washing the icon; the real 1.12 client
        looks the same way (director-checked, 1392), so this is taste, not fidelity, and the
        director chose the pet button's proportions instead:

        · the shine pane squared on the button — 37x37 at CENTER (0,0), scale 1.48 — so the rim
          runs ON the viewport edge (1.024x, the pet button's own ratio) and the tile's cell, the
          widget's own scissor, halves every star; and so the glow and the brackets share a centre
          (1393's "top and right are off" was the reference's own +1,+1);
        · the corner brackets at 71.53 rather than the reference's 60 — the art fills 33/64 of
          UI-AutoCastableOverlay.blp, and 71.53 = 37 x 58/30 puts the bracket square on this
          button's corners at the pet button's 0.997x.

        Reverting the widget to 1.12 exactly is: overlay 60, pane 36x36 CENTER (1,1), scale 1.22 —
        i.e. deleting this file. Nothing else here: the reference's file is sourced unedited.
    -->
    <Script><![CDATA[
        for i = 1, 12 do
            local button = getglobal("SpellButton" .. i)
            local overlay = getglobal("SpellButton" .. i .. "AutoCastable")
            overlay:SetWidth(71.53)
            overlay:SetHeight(71.53)
            local pane = getglobal("SpellButton" .. i .. "AutoCast")
            pane:SetWidth(37)
            pane:SetHeight(37)
            pane:ClearAllPoints()
            pane:SetPoint("CENTER", button, "CENTER", 0, 0)
            pane:SetModelScale(1.48)
        end
    ]]></Script>
</Ui>
